{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-340367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We begin by using the half-angle identity\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are not orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4106fd00c7c09eb2e47957e9f554a4749bd3a256ecd9a5434524d87c5b1e5f9"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "are not orthogonal"] ["text" "are orthogonal"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340367" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "are not orthogonal"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{18}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-9\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(0-0)+\\frac{1}{18}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4106fd00c7c09eb2e47957e9f554a4749bd3a256ecd9a5434524d87c5b1e5f9"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "are not orthogonal"] ["text" "are orthogonal"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340368" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "are orthogonal"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)={x}^{4}-7x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4106fd00c7c09eb2e47957e9f554a4749bd3a256ecd9a5434524d87c5b1e5f9"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340645" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{1}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4106fd00c7c09eb2e47957e9f554a4749bd3a256ecd9a5434524d87c5b1e5f9"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}"] ["math" "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\pi }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-340652" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-341340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ \n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-341340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/state.json" "file_sha256" "0a4ed507fc55a22a755e1ee513df96ceee2d9c6956c30559722b866c093f7b57"} {"question" "q-341340" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14063221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c4106fd00c7c09eb2e47957e9f554a4749bd3a256ecd9a5434524d87c5b1e5f9"} {"question" "q-341